Subject: [PATCH] Restore 2 file(s) my own ruff commit deleted

R0423, and I am the one who broke it. The trading box runs its own scheduled git
writers against this worktree, so the index is never mine alone. My first staging
pass hit `index.lock` partway through and left 47 paths staged; the retry added the
test files and committed EVERYTHING the index held -- including deletions the box's
writers had staged. ea3344f749 therefore removed files it had no business touching, among
them the cycle builder's work landed minutes earlier.

Restored from ea3344f749^ by explicit path:
  desks/mt5/scripts/widen_hourly_core_window.ps1
  scripts/check_own_clock_legs.py

The lesson is not "be careful with git add" -- it is that `git commit` on a shared
worktree commits the INDEX, not your edits, so the only safe pattern here is to
verify `git diff --cached --name-only` against your own intended list immediately
before committing, and abort on any path you did not put there.

